NNAAMMEE
     dduummmmyynneett — traffic shaper, bandwidth manager and delay emulator

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The dduummmmyynneett system facility permits the control of traffic going through
     the various network interfaces, by applying bandwidth and queue size lim‐
     itations, implementing different scheduling and queue management poli‐
     cies, and emulating delays and losses.

     The user interface for dduummmmyynneett is implemented by the dnctl(8) utility,
     so please refer to the dnctl(8) manpage for a complete description of the
     dduummmmyynneett capabilities and how to use it.

   KKeerrnneell OOppttiioonnss
     The following options in the kernel configuration file are related to
     dduummmmyynneett operation:

           IPFIREWALL                enable ipfirewall (if dduummmmyynneett is to be
                                     used with ipfw)
           IPFIREWALL_VERBOSE        enable firewall output
           IPFIREWALL_VERBOSE_LIMIT  limit firewall output
           DUMMYNET                  enable dduummmmyynneett operation
           HZ                        set the timer granularity

     Generally, the following options are required:

           options IPFIREWALL
           options DUMMYNET
           options HZ=1000         # strongly recommended

     Additionally, one may want to increase the number of mbuf clusters (used
     to store network packets) according to the sum of the bandwidth-delay
     products and queue sizes of all configured pipes.

